/-
# Centralizers in infinite locally finite simple groups (Kourovka Notebook Problem 5.18)

Kourovka Notebook, Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 5.18 (O. H. Kegel): let G be an infinite
locally finite simple group; is the centralizer of every element of G infinite?
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.Subgroup.Centralizer
public import WantedExt.GroupTheory.GroupClassesShared

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.LocallyFiniteSimpleCentralizersKourovka5Problem18Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 5.18 (O. H.
Kegel). UnsolvedMath record UM-00700302 (`KOU-5.18`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

Locally finite (the subgroup generated by every finite set is finite) is `IsLocallyFinite` of
`GroupClassesShared`; simple is Mathlib's `IsSimpleGroup`.
-/

open MathlibExt.GroupTheory.GroupClassesShared (IsLocallyFinite)

/-- Kourovka 5.18 (O. H. Kegel): in an infinite locally finite simple group, the centralizer of
every element is infinite. -/
def locallyFiniteSimpleCentralizersInfinite : Prop :=
  ∀ (G : Type) [Group G] [IsSimpleGroup G] [Infinite G], IsLocallyFinite G →
    ∀ g : G, (Subgroup.centralizer {g} : Set G).Infinite

/--
Resolved true: the Kourovka Archive answers 5.18 "Yes, it is", citing Hartley and Kuzucuoğlu,
Centralizers of elements in locally finite simple groups (Proc. London Math. Soc. (3) 62 (1991),
301-324). Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The
Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 5.18
(O. H. Kegel); resolution: B. Hartley and M. Kuzucuoğlu, Centralizers of elements in locally finite
simple groups, Proc. London Math. Soc. (3) 62 (1991), 301-324, Kourovka Archive, Problem 5.18: Yes,
it is (Hartley-Kuzucuoğlu); the theorem as stated in M. Kuzucuoğlu, Centralizers in simple locally
finite groups, Int. J. Group Theory 2 (2013), no. 1, 1-10, Theorem 2.7 (Hartley-Kuzucuoğlu): in an
infinite locally finite simple group the centralizer of every element is infinite,
https://doi.org/10.1112/plms/s3-62.2.301.
-/
public theorem_wanted locallyFiniteSimpleCentralizersInfinite_holds :
    locallyFiniteSimpleCentralizersInfinite

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.LocallyFiniteSimpleCentralizersKourovka5Problem18Wanted
